Note that `none` needs its OWN `no` form: `no mirror interface none`. `no mirror interface
port1.0.10` removed only the port-based entry (step 3) and left the `none` entry in place. The
advisory `% ` line fired on both entries into interface mode, as it does whenever any mirror
exists on the port, so the teardown was run WITHOUT `--stop-on-error` and gated on proven state.

