VERDICT: PASS -- `mirror interface none` exists on the x960, was accepted on port1.0.11, and was
reported by `show mirror` as a destination-only mirror (`Monitored Port Name: none (via ACL)`,
direction `receive`). It was proven to be an INDEPENDENT and PERSISTENT declaration: it coexists
with a port-based mirror on the same port, survives that mirror's removal, and needs its own
`no mirror interface none` to clear. Teardown left the running-config byte-identical to the
pre-group baseline. PROVEN: the `none` form exists, is accepted, is reported, persists, and is
separately removable. NOT MEASURED: any actual mirroring behaviour -- `none` sources its traffic
from a hardware ACL and no ACL and no traffic were involved, and port1.0.10/port1.0.11 are empty
SFP cages with no link (I-9). DRAFTED EXPECTATION NOT MET: the draft says `show mirror` should
report "no active mirror"; it does not, and it should not -- `none` means "no SOURCE interface
(set destination interface only)", not "no mirror". That is a reconstruction error (I-4), not a
product defect, and the graded PASS rests on that reading. IF THE REAL AWPTCM TEXT ASSERTS THAT
`none` DEACTIVATES THE MIRROR, RE-GRADE THIS TO FAIL -- the verbatim evidence for that call is in
STEP 2.
